detector_raw:
{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "What is the objective you want the production plan to optimize—maximize total profit, maximize total revenue, or something else?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the optimization objective, which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For each ton of product A and product B produced, how many tons of the raw materials are blended together to make one ton of finished product?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for the specific raw material composition (recipe) for both products in a single sentence. Since it requests the same type of information (input quantities per unit output) for the two items in one unified request, it counts as one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Should I assume that one ton of each finished product is made from exactly one ton of raw materials combined (i.e., the blend inputs sum to one ton per ton of product)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for confirmation of a specific mass balance assumption."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since the blend ratio is not yet confirmed, would you like me to build the model with a clearly labeled placeholder assumption (one ton of raw materials per ton of product) that you can adjust later?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single yes/no clarification question about whether to proceed with a specific placeholder assumption."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Who is the right person or team to confirm the blend ratio, so I can note it as an open item in the plan?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification request asking for the identity of the person or team responsible for confirming the blend ratio."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Can we proceed by treating the blend ratio as a decision variable that the model will choose, rather than a fixed number you must confirm first?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for a policy choice on how to handle the blend ratio."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Would you like me to pause the modeling and instead give you a short list of the specific blend-ratio questions you need answered internally before the plan can be finalized?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single yes/no clarification question asking whether the user wants to pause modeling to receive a list of internal questions."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is the blend ratio the only unresolved item, or are there other inputs (such as production costs beyond raw material purchase, or capacity limits) that also still need internal confirmation?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether the blend ratio is the only unresolved item or if other inputs also need confirmation."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since the blend ratio cannot be confirmed now, should I proceed to build the model using the standard assumption that each ton of product requires one ton of raw materials in total, clearly labeled as an assumption to be revisited?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for permission to proceed with a specific assumption."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Would it be acceptable for me to deliver the plan as a parametric model—showing the profit-maximizing solution as a function of the blend ratio—so that once the ratio is confirmed internally, you can plug it in without rebuilding the model?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for approval on the delivery format of the plan."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Do you want me to stop asking about the blend ratio and instead deliver the best possible plan under a clearly stated assumption, so you have something concrete to react to internally?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for a decision on whether to proceed with an assumption-based plan."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "If it would help, I can also hand you a one-page list of the exact questions to bring to that internal discussion (e.g., mass balance, yield losses, whether D is a blend component or an additive). Just say the word."
  ],
  "rationale": "The response concludes with a conditional offer to provide a list of questions, which functions as a clarification request for the user to confirm if they want that additional output. The rest of the text is explanatory and does not contain other independent questions."
}
